From 1e54a6dde5245e65d30cfece8b8bd7345d524831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barattolo <barattolo@barattolo.store>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] timeout: the maker's wait for the hold invoice is never
 longer than the time to pay he chose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0011 gives the maker of an order a waiting window of his own
(`maker_expiration_seconds`, three hours on this node), because he cannot
know when his order will be taken. A seller who sets a short time to pay
on the timer (patch 0013) tells the buyer he trades fast; the buyer must
not then wait three hours for his hold invoice.

For a sell order in `waiting-payment`, the payment-window job now asks the
marketplace server the time to pay the maker chose — the same request,
answered in a second table, `{"pubblica": {id: seconds}}`, checked like
the buyer's window (whole minutes, 900..86400) — and keeps it in a side
table, `barattolo_maker_windows`, out of the migrations and pruned once
the order leaves the book and the waiting states. The maker's window on
that order is the shorter of his own and his choice: in
`find_order_by_seconds` (the cutoff follows the shortest choice) and in
`reconfirm_timeout_eligibility`. When it lapses, patch 0011 runs as
before (back to the book, removed at the limit).

A server without the table, an id it leaves out, or an unreadable side
table all mean "no choice": the maker keeps his own window. The info
event carries `barattolo_maker_payment_window = 1` next to
`barattolo_payment_windows`.
